WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:03.877
<v Examiner>Erection, the breast, and her female words.

2
00:00:03.877 --> 00:00:04.738
<v Examiner>The fine print.

3
00:00:05.188 --> 00:00:10.276
The last of the fine print: her erection steps, which she asks as put-them-in-order,

4
00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:15.727
the breast, from her lactation case quiz, and her two big matching tables of female words.

5
00:00:16.177 --> 00:00:19.902
The hook: nitric oxide, widen, flow, fill, and drain.

6
00:00:19.902 --> 00:00:22.714
The breast sits on the pectoralis major.

7
00:00:22.714 --> 00:00:24.753
And pregnancy is forty weeks.

8
00:00:25.203 --> 00:00:26.925
Her erection steps, in order.

9
00:00:26.925 --> 00:00:31.915
It starts with a thought or an action triggering the parasympathetic nervous system.

10
00:00:31.915 --> 00:00:34.647
Then nitric oxide, a vasodilator, is released.

11
00:00:34.647 --> 00:00:39.815
The central artery, the other arterioles, and the mesh of spongy erectile tissue widen.

12
00:00:39.815 --> 00:00:43.795
More blood flows through the central artery into the spongy tissue.

13
00:00:43.795 --> 00:00:48.191
The corpora cavernosa fill with blood and press against their outer walls,

14
00:00:48.191 --> 00:00:52.586
squashing the veins, so blood can't flow back out, and the penis is rigid.

15
00:00:52.586 --> 00:00:55.735
Last, the blood is redirected back out into the body,

16
00:00:55.735 --> 00:00:58.289
and the penis returns to its flaccid state.

17
00:00:58.289 --> 00:01:01.021
In her numbering: two, five, four, three, one.

18
00:01:01.471 --> 00:01:03.051
Her male true or falses.

19
00:01:03.051 --> 00:01:06.738
An enlarged testicle can make it hard to urinate: false.

20
00:01:06.738 --> 00:01:12.532
It's an enlarged prostate that does that, because the prostate wraps around the urethra.

21
00:01:12.532 --> 00:01:15.955
Men have only one opening for urine and semen: true.

22
00:01:15.955 --> 00:01:21.683
The prostaglandins from the seminal vesicles bring on involuntary peristalsis of smooth

23
00:01:21.683 --> 00:01:27.410
muscle in both the male and the female tracts, helping sperm reach the fallopian tubes:

24
00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:27.739
true.

25
00:01:27.739 --> 00:01:32.019
Semen is produced by the seminal vesicles and the prostate, both.

26
00:01:32.019 --> 00:01:35.376
Males secrete testosterone, FSH, and LH: all three.

27
00:01:35.376 --> 00:01:40.248
And if testosterone doesn't work during the development of a male's brain,

28
00:01:40.248 --> 00:01:45.449
the brain might have a female orientation, or gender identity may be ambiguous.

29
00:01:45.449 --> 00:01:46.634
Both are possible.

30
00:01:48.084 --> 00:01:50.289
The breast, her lactation case quiz.

31
00:01:50.289 --> 00:01:53.720
The breast sits directly on the pectoralis major muscle,

32
00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:58.437
over the intercostal muscles and the ribs, and her diagram adds the clavicle,

33
00:01:58.437 --> 00:02:00.520
part of the appendicular skeleton.

34
00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:04.073
Inside are adipose tissue, the lobules with their alveoli,

35
00:02:04.073 --> 00:02:07.687
which make milk under prolactin, and the lactiferous ducts,

36
00:02:07.687 --> 00:02:11.118
which release it under oxytocin, and open at the nipple.

37
00:02:11.118 --> 00:02:15.406
The areola, the dark area round the nipple, contains sebaceous glands,

38
00:02:15.406 --> 00:02:16.938
and darkens in pregnancy.

39
00:02:16.938 --> 00:02:21.716
The nipple contains erectile tissue, and hardens by smooth muscle contraction,

40
00:02:21.716 --> 00:02:23.860
in response to sympathetic stimuli.

41
00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:28.588
Oestrogen is responsible for primary breast development, at puberty.

42
00:02:28.588 --> 00:02:33.181
Progesterone is responsible for further breast development, in pregnancy.

43
00:02:33.181 --> 00:02:37.773
Her true or false: breast development is a primary sexual characteristic.

44
00:02:37.773 --> 00:02:39.535
False: it's a secondary one.

45
00:02:39.535 --> 00:02:43.813
Another: breasts are well supported by strong ligaments and muscles.

46
00:02:43.813 --> 00:02:44.191
False.

47
00:02:44.191 --> 00:02:48.972
The breast has no muscle of its own: it hangs from its suspensory ligaments.

48
00:02:48.972 --> 00:02:52.432
That reason is the podcast's, but the false is her key.

49
00:02:52.432 --> 00:02:57.969
And her case: a woman who isn't pregnant takes high doses of oestrogen and progesterone,

50
00:02:57.969 --> 00:02:59.164
and then prolactin.

51
00:02:59.164 --> 00:03:01.366
Her mammary glands begin lactating.

52
00:03:02.816 --> 00:03:05.462
Her female words, two big matching tables.

53
00:03:05.462 --> 00:03:08.485
Ovulation: the release of an egg from the ovary.

54
00:03:08.485 --> 00:03:11.509
Fertilisation: the fusion of an egg and a sperm.

55
00:03:11.509 --> 00:03:15.162
Contraception: a procedure or device to prevent pregnancy.

56
00:03:15.162 --> 00:03:18.752
Menstruation: the shedding of the endometrium each month.

57
00:03:18.752 --> 00:03:21.398
It's the stratum functionalis that's shed,

58
00:03:21.398 --> 00:03:25.051
after the spiral arteries constrict and cut off its blood.

59
00:03:25.051 --> 00:03:30.091
Pregnancy: the forty weeks during which a new individual develops in the mother.

60
00:03:30.091 --> 00:03:35.634
And abortion: the termination of a pregnancy by the removal or expulsion of an embryo or

61
00:03:35.634 --> 00:03:36.075
foetus.

62
00:03:36.525 --> 00:03:37.736
The organs, her way.

63
00:03:37.736 --> 00:03:40.462
The uterus is a hollow, pear-shaped, elastic,

64
00:03:40.462 --> 00:03:44.824
muscular structure where a fertilised ovum can grow to a full-term baby.

65
00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:48.095
The ovary is a gland that makes oestrogen and oocytes.

66
00:03:48.095 --> 00:03:50.942
The placenta forms on the inside of the uterus,

67
00:03:50.942 --> 00:03:55.122
and takes oxygen and nutrients from the mother's blood to the foetus,

68
00:03:55.122 --> 00:03:56.758
through the umbilical cord.

69
00:03:56.758 --> 00:04:01.423
And one secondary sexual characteristic promoted by oestrogen, from her quiz:

70
00:04:01.423 --> 00:04:03.725
enlargement of the external genitalia.

71
00:04:04.175 --> 00:04:04.845
The traps.

72
00:04:04.845 --> 00:04:08.732
The steps of an erection end with blood draining back out.

73
00:04:08.732 --> 00:04:12.954
An enlarged prostate, not a testicle, makes it hard to urinate.

74
00:04:12.954 --> 00:04:15.970
Breast development is secondary, not primary.

75
00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:17.913
And pregnancy is forty weeks.

76
